hould be back in action.\n\n### My Tonie/Creative Tonie is not playing the updated content on the Toniebox 2\n\nIf you have edited the audio content on your Tonie or Creative Tonie but your Toniebox 2 is still playing the old content, there are two possible reasons for this: Your Toniebox 2 isn’t connected to Wi-Fi: Check whether your Toniebox 2 is connected to Wi-Fi. To do this, open the tonies app and tap o...--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-nz/articles/29422120806546-Tapping-the-Toniebox-2-to-skip-forward-and-back-isn-t-working)\nciteturn1005search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; # Tapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\n# Tapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\nIf your Toniebox 2 isn’t skipping tracks when you give it a tap, don’t worry—it may just need to turn off and back on again. Your Toniebox 2 will turn off automatically on its own after five minutes of no activity. When it wakes up again, the tapping magic should be back in action.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nToniebox 2 – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-gb/sections/29036371272594-Toniebox-2)\nciteturn1005search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; ### Will our existing Tonies work on the Toniebox 2? ... ### Tapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\n10 articles\n\n### How do I restart the Toniebox 2?\n\nRead Article →\n\n### How to reset your Toniebox 2 to factory settings\n\nRead Article →\n\n### My Toniebox 2 is stuck, what do I do?\n\nRead Article →\n\n### What can I do if my Toniebox 2 isn’t turning on?\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Why does my Toniebox 2 not play a Tonie when it is plugged in?\n\nRead Article →\n\n### My Tonie isn't playing\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Tonie is playing the audio from a different Tonie\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Toniebox 2 download speed seems slow\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Tapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\nRead Article →\n\n### My Tonie/Creative Tonie is not playing the updated content on the Toniebox 2\n\nRead Article →\n\n## Error Codes\n\n12 articles\n\n### Code Word: Squirrel\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Frog\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Rabbit\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Parrot\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Dog\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Tiger\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Horse\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Cat\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Llama\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Zebra\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Sheep\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Fox\n\nRead Article →--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTroubleshooting – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-150/sections/29258108517522-Troubleshooting)\nciteturn1005search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; ### Tapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\n# Troubleshooting\n\n## Articles\n\n10 articles\n\n### How do I restart the Toniebox 2?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### How to reset your Toniebox 2 to factory settings\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### My Toniebox 2 is stuck, what do I do?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### What can I do if my Toniebox 2 isn’t turning on?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Why does my Toniebox 2 not play a Tonie when it is plugged in?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### My Tonie isn't playing\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Tonie is playing the audio from a different Tonie\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Toniebox 2 download speed seems slow\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Tapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### My Tonie/Creative Tonie is not playing the updated content on the Toniebox 2\n\nRead Full Article →--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTapping the Toniebox to skip forward and back isn't working – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-150/articles/29036632245650-Tapping-the-Toniebox-to-skip-forward-and-back-isn-t-working)\nciteturn1005search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # Tapping the Toniebox to skip forward and back isn't working ... Another important note is that some users have lovingly referred to the tapping feature as more of a 'whack', as a fair amount of force is required, rather than a light tap on either side of the Toniebox.\n\n# Tapping the Toniebox to skip forward and back isn't working\n\n# Overview\n\nAre you having trouble skipping between chapters? It's important to note that the Tonie's content must be fully downloaded before you can skip forward and back. If you are still running into some trouble, place your Tonie on top of your Toniebox and let's take a look at the Toniebox LED:\n\n# Visual Cues\n\nLED Visual  | Suggestion\n--- | ---\nImage: Dec-20-2018_12-18-51.gif\nFlashing Blue  | \n\n  * A flashing blue LED means that your Tonie's content has not been fully downloaded. This typically takes just a few minutes. Wait until the LED lights up solid green, then you are good to go!\nImage: green.gif\nGlowing Green  | \n\n  * If you are still unable to skip when the LED is solid green, make sure the tilt and tap feature is enabled in your Toniebox settings*\n \n  * Does your Creative-Tonie only have one chapter? In this instance you can only rewind or fast forward by tilting the Toniebox. Once you have more content (chapters) uploaded, you can tap to skip! \n\n \n\n# Pro Tips\n\nAnother important note is that some users have lovingly referred to the tapping feature as more of a 'whack', as a fair amount of force is required, rather than a light tap on either side of the Toniebox. Once the Toniebox LED is solid green, give it a try and you will become an expert in no time!\n\n# Here's How\n\n## Video Instructions\n\nUsing the tonies® app\n\nImage: Youtube video preview image\n\n### We need your consent to load the Youtube service!\n\nWe use a third party service to embed video content that may collect data about your activity. Please review the details and accept the service to watch this video.\n\nThis content is not permitted to load due to trackers that are not disclosed to the visitor. The website owner needs to setup the site with their CMP to add this content to the list of technologies used.\n\n[Button: More Information ][Button: Accept ]\n\nPowered by Usercentrics Consent Management Platform\n\n## Step-by-Step Guide\n\n  1. ### Open Your Collection\n\nOpen the tonies® app and tap the icon in the bottom right hand corner titled 'Collection'.\nImage: Step_1.jpg\n\n  2. ### Find your Toniebox\n\nTap on the 'Toniebox' header.\nImage: Wifi1__1_.jpg\n \n\n  3. ### Select your Toniebox\n\nTap on the picture of the Toniebox you would like to make changes to.\nImage: wifi3__1_.jpg\n \n\n  4. ### Access Advanced Settings\n\nScroll down and tap on 'Advanced settings' at the bottom of the screen.\nImage: 1__3_.jpg\n \n\n  5. ### Turn on 'Tilt and tap'\n\nHere is where you can enable the tap and tilt feature. Tap the 'Off' toggle to turn this feature on.\nImage: TapTiltOff.jpg\n \n\n  6. ### Sync your changes\n\nOnce you are finished making changes, you will just need to sync the Toniebox with your Wi-Fi to make sure that it receives the news that changes have been made. To do this, turn on the Toniebox and then pinch one of the Tonieboxes ears for about three seconds until you hear a sound and the LED begins flashing blue. The Toniebox LED will flash blue for a few seconds while it updates with the new changes. Once the LED turns solid green, you are ready to go! Any new changes should now be reflected properly.\nImage: 4.jpg\n \n\nStill running into some trouble? Send us a message including your Toniebox ID and we will get to the bottom of it!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTroubleshooting – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/sections/29258108517522-Troubleshooting)\nciteturn1005search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; If you want to change this setting, simply open the tonies® app, tap on your Toniebox 2, select settings and the scroll to \"Age Mode\" to change from 1+ to 3+. ... ### Tapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\n### What can I do if my Toniebox 2 isn’t turning on?\n\nIf giving it a good old telling off hasn’t worked (we assume you’ve tried), then here are some suggestions of where to go next: You might need to restart your Toniebox. Here’s a little guide to walk you through it. If that doesn’t fix it, try giving your Toniebox a full recharge. It takes about 4 ho...\n\n### Why does my Toniebox 2 not play a Tonie when it is plugged in?\n\nThis is expected behaviour when your Toniebox 2 is set to 1+ mode. If you want to change this setting, simply open the tonies® app, tap on your Toniebox 2, select settings and the scroll to \"Age Mode\" to change from 1+ to 3+.\n\n### My Tonie isn't playing\n\nSome Toniebox 2 customers have had trouble downloading Tonies recently. The issue has now been fixed, but you’ll need to update your Toniebox 2 to make sure everything runs smoothly. Here’s how to do it: Switch on your Toniebox 2. Wait until it turns off again by itself. Switch it back on. Wait for ...\n\n### Tonie is playing the audio from a different Tonie\n\nIf the Toniebox 2 starts playing audio from another Tonie, don’t worry—your little one has likely just swapped their Tonies too quickly. This is an easy fix: simply remove the Tonie from the Toniebox 2, wait a few seconds, and then place the desired Tonie back on top to resume the listening fun.\n\n### Toniebox 2 download speed seems slow\n\nWhen you place a new Tonie or Tonieplay Disc on your Toniebox 2, the fun doesn’t always start instantly. Before your story, song, or audi