a\n\nRead Article →\n\n### Code Word: Sheep\n\nRead Article →--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTapping the Toniebox 1 to skip forward and back isn't working – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-nz/articles/29036632245650-Tapping-the-Toniebox-1-to-skip-forward-and-back-isn-t-working)\nciteturn1005search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; # Tapping the Toniebox 1 to skip forward and back isn't working ... Another important note is that some users have lovingly referred to the tapping feature as more of a 'whack', as a fair amount of force is required, rather than a light tap on either side of the Toniebox 1.\n\n# Tapping the Toniebox 1 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\n# Overview\n\nAre you having trouble skipping between chapters? It's important to note that the Tonie's content must be fully downloaded before you can skip forward and back. If you are still running into some trouble, place your Tonie on top of your Toniebox 1 and let's take a look at the Toniebox 1 LED:\n\n# Visual Cues\n\nLED Visual  | Suggestion\n--- | ---\nImage: Dec-20-2018_12-18-51.gif\nFlashing Blue  | \n\n  * A flashing blue LED means that your Tonie's content has not been fully downloaded. This typically takes just a few minutes. Wait until the LED lights up solid green, then you are good to go!\nImage: green.gif\nGlowing Green  | \n\n  * If you are still unable to skip when the LED is solid green, make sure the tilt and tap feature is enabled in your Toniebox 1 settings*\n \n  * Does your Creative-Tonie only have one chapter? In this instance you can only rewind or fast forward by tilting the Toniebox 1. Once you have more content (chapters) uploaded, you can tap to skip! \n\n# Pro Tips\n\nAnother important note is that some users have lovingly referred to the tapping feature as more of a 'whack', as a fair amount of force is required, rather than a light tap on either side of the Toniebox 1. Once the Toniebox 1 LED is solid green, give it a try and you will become an expert in no time!\n\n# Here's How\n\n## Step-by-Step Guide\n\n  1. ### Open Your Collection\n\nOpen the tonies® app and tap the icon in the bottom right hand corner titled 'Collection'.\nImage: Step_1.jpg\n\n  2. ### Find your Toniebox 1\n\nTap on the 'Toniebox' header.\nImage: Wifi1__1_.jpg\n \n\n  3. ### Select your Toniebox 1\n\nTap on the picture of the Toniebox 1 you would like to make changes to.\nImage: wifi3__1_.jpg\n \n\n  4. ### Access Advanced Settings\n\nScroll down and tap on 'Advanced settings' at the bottom of the screen.\nImage: 1__3_.jpg\n \n\n  5. ### Turn on 'Tilt and tap'\n\nHere is where you can enable the tap and tilt feature. Tap the 'Off' toggle to turn this feature on.\nImage: TapTiltOff.jpg\n \n\n  6. ### Sync your changes\n\nOnce you are finished making changes, you will just need to sync the Toniebox 1 with your Wi-Fi to make sure that it receives the news that changes have been made. To do this, turn on the Toniebox 1and then pinch one of the Tonieboxes ears for about three seconds until you hear a sound and the LED begins flashing blue. The Toniebox 1 LED will flash blue for a few seconds while it updates with the new changes. Once the LED turns solid green, you are ready to go! Any new changes should now be reflected properly.\n\nStill running into some trouble? Send us a message including your Toniebox 1 ID and we will get to the bottom of it!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nToniebox 1 – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-nz/sections/29036371188498-Toniebox-1)\nciteturn1005search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; ### Does the Toniebox 1 work without Wi-Fi? ... ### Tapping the Toniebox 1 to skip forward and back isn't working ... 2 articles\n\n# Toniebox 1\n\n### Popular Articles\n\nToniebox 1\n\nBrowse Topic\n\nQuick Search\n\n[Input: Search for articles, guides, and help...]\n\n### Topics\n\nQuick Solutions Setu